Chapter: Fuel

 A FuelResult is one of FuelOk or FuelExhausted.
 To fuel-ok gives a FuelOk wrapping the given value.
 To fuel-map gives a new FuelResult by applying a function to the value inside FuelOk, or FuelExhausted unchanged.
 To fuel-bind gives a new FuelResult by chaining a function over a FuelOk, or FuelExhausted unchanged.
 To fuel-check gives FuelOk with the remaining fuel decremented, or FuelExhausted when fuel reaches zero.

 We say:

Section: Fuel State

  FuelResult (a) =
    | FuelOk (a)
    | FuelExhausted

  fuel-ok : a -> FuelResult a
  fuel-ok (v) = FuelOk v

  fuel-map : (a -> b), FuelResult a -> FuelResult b
  fuel-map (f) (r) = when r
    is FuelOk (v) -> FuelOk (f v)
    is FuelExhausted -> FuelExhausted

  fuel-bind : FuelResult a, (a -> FuelResult b) -> FuelResult b
  fuel-bind (r) (f) = when r
    is FuelOk (v) -> f v
    is FuelExhausted -> FuelExhausted

  fuel-check : Integer -> FuelResult Integer
  fuel-check (remaining) =
    if remaining <= 0 then FuelExhausted
    else FuelOk (remaining - 1)
